The prompt’s guarantee makes this a bisection problem: an even number of coefficients gives an odd-degree polynomial, and a nonzero leading coefficient forces opposite signs far enough to the left and right. I’m using integer literals plus `/` so the K model can give division exact rational meaning while Python still returns the expected floating-point approximation.

